A loader validates order line records batch by batch; the rules it applies and the next batch (16 records) are shown below. Either every rule holds or exactly one is broken, at one spot. Nothing is a violation unless a listed rule, taken literally, forbids it.

Record fields: line_id (text), unit_price (whole number), gift_note (text), pickup_point (text), gift (text), placed_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), discount_pct (whole number), quantity (whole number), order_no (text), sku (text), weight_kg (whole number), tier (text), line_total (whole number), delivery_zone (text), replaces (text), shipped_on (date, YYYY-MM-DD), warehouse (text).

Integrity rules:
R1. The allowed span of `discount_pct` depends on `tier`: 8 to 35 for "trade", 0 to 12 for "retail", limits included.
R2. `weight_kg` is never smaller than 5 and never larger than 30.
R3. `placed_on` precedes `shipped_on`, and the two never coincide.
R4. A record whose `gift` is "yes" needs a filled-in `gift_note`; for other records `gift_note` is optional.
R5. Within the batch, all values of `line_id` differ from one another.
R6. `replaces` may be empty; otherwise it holds a `line_id` found in one of the records above it.
R7. The stored `line_total` has to match `quantity` x `unit_price`.
R8. A combination of `sku` and `order_no` that turns up in two records is not allowed, although each of the two fields may repeat by itself.
R9. A `warehouse` is valid only if the reference list `warehouses` holds it and marks it "active".

Reference list `warehouses` with 9 entries (key: status): WH-15: inactive; WH-23: active; WH-35: active; WH-40: suspended; WH-50: active; WH-62: suspended; WH-74: active; WH-83: suspended; WH-85: active

Statuses in a reference list: a rule that only asks for a key of the list accepts every key the list holds, whatever its status; only a rule that names a status requires it.

